}},"correct_choice":"b","rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. The line of best fit passes through the point <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"with coordinates 8,500 comma 39\"></span>. Therefore, the line of best fit predicts a temperature of 39&deg;F for a location in Lake Tahoe Basin with an elevation of 8,500 feet.<p>Choice A is incorrect. This is the lowest temperature listed on the scatterplot, and the line of best fit never crosses this value for any of the elevations shown. Choice C is incorrect. According to the line of best fit, the temperature of 41&deg;F is predicted for an elevation of slightly greater than 7,500 feet, not an elevation of 8,500 feet. Choice D is incorrect. According to the line of best fit, the temperature of 43&deg;F is predicted for an elevation of roughly 6,700 feet, not an elevation of 8,500 feet.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959633,"updateDate":1691007959633}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959633, 1691007959633),
    ($SATQ$ad1d6adb$SATQ$, $SATQ$cb21253d-b0c2-4157-bf21-8fa351eb6b79$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Percentages$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The number of coins in a collection increased from <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math> to <math alttext="90"><mn>90</mn>
</math>. What was the percent increase in the number of coins in this collection?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"339b68f8-be91-44d9-aafc-937af56ec49f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"10 percent sign\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"5d73d048-0f58-4d44-86c3-48542020fcb9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"81 percent sign\"><mn>81</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"654eab99-1538-455b-8e5f-c94a89653d2f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"90 percent sign\"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"713c9afc-38ee-4574-a6bc-3a2ed80b6b79","content":"<p><math alttext=\"900 percent sign\"><mn>900</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["D"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["713c9afc-38ee-4574-a6bc-3a2ed80b6b79"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is correct. It's given that the number of coins in the collection increased from <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math> to <math alttext="90"><mn>90</mn>
</math>. It follows that the number of coins in the collection increased by <math alttext="90 minus 9"><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math>, or <math alttext="81"><mn>81</mn>
</math>. Let <math alttext="x percent sign"><mi>x</mi><mo>%</mo></math> represent the percentage that <math alttext="81"><mn>81</mn>
</math> is of <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math>. The value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> can be found using the proportion <math alttext="StartFraction 81 Over 9 EndFraction equals StartFraction x Over 100 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>81</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math>, or&nbsp;<math alttext="9 equals StartFraction x Over 100 EndFraction"><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></math>. Multiplying both sides of this equation by <math alttext="100"><mn>100</mn>
</math> yields&nbsp;<math alttext="900 equals x"><mn>900</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math>. Thus, when the number of coins in the collection increased from <math alttext="9"><mn>9</mn>
</math> to <math alttext="90"><mn>90</mn>
</math>, the percent increase was <math alttext="900 percent sign"><mn>900</mn><mo>%</mo></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ad1d6adb","external_id":"cb21253d-b0c2-4157-bf21-8fa351eb6b79","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"e3176ba8-fa53-47f7-935a-0a0a8b579b82","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.B.","skill_desc":"Percentages","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The number of coins in a collection increased from <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math> to <math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math>. What was the percent increase in the number of coins in this collection?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"339b68f8-be91-44d9-aafc-937af56ec49f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"10 percent sign\"><mn>10</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"5d73d048-0f58-4d44-86c3-48542020fcb9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"81 percent sign\"><mn>81</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"654eab99-1538-455b-8e5f-c94a89653d2f","content":"<p><math alttext=\"90 percent sign\"><mn>90</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"713c9afc-38ee-4574-a6bc-3a2ed80b6b79","content":"<p><math alttext=\"900 percent sign\"><mn>900</mn><mo>%</mo></math></p>"}],"keys":["713c9afc-38ee-4574-a6bc-3a2ed80b6b79"],"correct_answer":["D"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is correct. It's given that the number of coins in the collection increased from <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math> to <math alttext=\"90\"><mn>90</mn>\n</math>. It follows that the number of coins in the collection increased by <math alttext=\"90 minus 9\"><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"81\"><mn>81</mn>\n</math>. Let <math alttext=\"x percent sign\"><mi>x</mi><mo>%</mo></math> represent the percentage that <math alttext=\"81\"><mn>81</mn>\n</math> is of <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</