<div role="region" aria-label="Long description for scatterplot" class="sr-only"><ul><li>The scatterplot has 11 data points.</li>
<li>The data points are in a linear pattern trending up from left to right.</li>
<li>A line of best fit is shown:<br>
<ul>
<li>The line of best fit slants up from left to right.</li>
<li>5 points are above the line of best fit.</li>
<li>6 points are below the line of best fit.</li>
<li>The line of best fit passes through the following approximate coordinates:<br>
<ul>
<li>(2 comma 2.9)</li>
<li>(8 comma 7.7)</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul></div></figure></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The scatterplot shows the relationship between two variables, <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> and <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>. A line of best fit is also shown. For how many of the <math alttext="11"><mn>11</mn>
</math> data points does the line of best fit predict a greater <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>-value than the actual <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>-value?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["6"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["6"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math>. The line of best fit predicts a greater <em>y</em>-value than the actual <em>y</em>-value for any data point that's located below the line of best fit. For the scatterplot shown, <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> of the data points are below the line of best fit. Therefore, the line of best fit predicts a greater <em>y</em>-value than the actual <em>y</em>-value for <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> of the data points.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"ad7dbb22","external_id":"44d16b54-4d25-47d8-9c06-f7e06ccbc36f","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"821dc944-05d3-4a71-abc9-ac24f8450f98","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22pt\" version=\"1.1\" viewBox=\"0 0 286.56 275.22\" width=\"286.56pt\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"A scatterplot in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis ranges from 0 to 10. The y axis ranges from 0 to 10. Refer to long description.\">\n <defs>\n  <style type=\"text/css\">\n*{stroke-linecap:butt;stroke-linejoin:round;}\n  </style>\n </defs>\n <g id=\"figure_1\">\n  <g id=\"patch_1\">\n   <path d=\"M 0 275.22 \nL 286.56 275.22 \nL 286.56 0 \nL 0 0 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_1\">\n   <g id=\"patch_2\">\n    <path d=\"M 7.2 260.46 \nL 279.36 260.46 \nL 279.36 10.98 \nL 7.2 10.98 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"></g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_2\"></g>\n  </g>\n  <g id=\"axes_2\">\n   <g id=\"patch_3\">\n    <path d=\"M 9.200821 268.02 \nL 271.689179 268.02 \nL 271.689179 7.2 \nL 9.200821 7.2 \nz\n\" style=\"fill:none;\"></path>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_3\">\n    <g id=\"xtick_1\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_2\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_3\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_4\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_5\"></g>\n    <g id=\"xtick_6\"></g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"matplotlib.axis_4\">\n    <g id=\"ytick_1\"></g>\n    <g id=\"ytick_2\"></g>\n    <g id=\"ytick_3\"></g>\n    <g id=\"ytick_