" x=\"141.134404\" xlink:href=\"#m2b56e7b63d\" y=\"146.916957\"></use>\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"157.680105\" xlink:href=\"#m2b56e7b63d\" y=\"110.087452\"></use>\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"174.225807\" xlink:href=\"#m2b56e7b63d\" y=\"103.591732\"></use>\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"190.771508\" xlink:href=\"#m2b56e7b63d\" y=\"110.577695\"></use>\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"207.317209\" xlink:href=\"#m2b56e7b63d\" y=\"73.748189\"></use>\n     <use style=\"stroke:#000000;\" x=\"223.86291\" xlink:href=\"#m2b56e7b63d\" y=\"90.845414\"></use>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n   <g id=\"line2d_2\">\n    <path clip-path=\"url(#pf85b540db9)\" d=\"M 53.993711 206.51825 \nL 229.929668 65.769484 \nL 229.929668 65.769484 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"pf85b540db9\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"262.488358\" x=\"9.200821\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for scatterplot\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>The scatterplot has 11 data points.</li>\n<li>The data points are in a linear pattern trending up from left to right.</li>\n<li>A line of best fit is shown:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The line of best fit slants up from left to right.</li>\n<li>5 points are above the line of best fit.</li>\n<li>6 points are below the line of best fit.</li>\n<li>The line of best fit passes through the following approximate coordinates:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(2 comma 2.9)</li>\n<li>(8 comma 7.7)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The scatterplot shows the relationship between two variables, <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>. A line of best fit is also shown. For how many of the <math alttext=\"11\"><mn>11</mn>\n</math> data points does the line of best fit predict a greater <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>-value than the actual <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>-value?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["6"],"correct_answer":["6"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>. The line of best fit predicts a greater <em>y</em>-value than the actual <em>y</em>-value for any data point that's located below the line of best fit. For the scatterplot shown, <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> of the data points are below the line of best fit. Therefore, the line of best fit predicts a greater <em>y</em>-value than the actual <em>y</em>-value for <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> of the data points.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357404,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"ad7dbb22","skill_cd":"Q.D.","score_band_range_cd":5,"skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","createDate":1730147357404,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"","external_id":"44d16b54-4d25-47d8-9c06-f7e06ccbc36f","primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"821dc944-05d3-4a71-abc9-ac24f8450f98","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[],"externalid":"44d16b54-4d25-47d8-9c06-f7e06ccbc36f","keys":["6"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>. The line of best fit predicts a greater <em>y</em>-value than the actual <em>y</em>-value for any data point that's located below the line of best fit. For the scatterplot shown, <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> of the data points are below the line of best fit. Therefore, the line of best fit predicts a greater <em>y</em>-value than the actual <em>y</em>-value for <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> of the data points.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg height=\"275.22p