</math> inches.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"aeeaec96","external_id":"ee5f324c-581b-4818-b0a7-48d75fb59f22","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"d1e4924e-9139-4be0-a21e-6b9d94b9bb4b","uId":"39f70188-fd9e-4026-ab10-07e6fc852152","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">How many <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">yards</span> are equivalent to <math alttext=\"612\"><mn>612</mn>\n</math> inches? <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 1 yard  equals 36 inches right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mtext>&#160;yard</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math></p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"1438bfb8-90af-4116-9a0d-e3d20ca2e178","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0.059\"><mn>0.059</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"095e601a-8b55-4b33-93f6-02cc5df4943c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"17\"><mn>17</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d32e8e29-fe22-4a75-a7ea-c78d63edb069","content":"<p><math alttext=\"576\"><mn>576</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5fe64a14-a495-4d39-b4b5-e98611488fcf","content":"<p><math alttext=\"22,032\"><mn>22,032</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["095e601a-8b55-4b33-93f6-02cc5df4943c"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. It&rsquo;s given that <math alttext=\"1 yard  equals 36 inches\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>yard</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</mtext></math>. Therefore, <math alttext=\"612\"><mn>612</mn>\n</math> inches&nbsp;is equivalent to <math alttext=\"612 inches left parenthesis StartFraction 1 yard Over 36 inches EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mn>612</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>inches</