he previous year. Therefore, Account A always earns at least $30 per year, which is more than the $25 per year that Account B earns.</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959638,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"af142f8d","skill_cd":"Q.D.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","createDate":1691007959638,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"11107-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"e19efa51-d808-428e-85da-10218c337977","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"11107-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\" class=\"stimulus_reference \">\n        <div class=\"table_wrapper \">\n          <table class=\"tcp-b0e3451f-e375-462b-864f-c033e7a24a62\"><tbody><tr><td>\n                  <table class=\"table_WithBorder\"><tbody class=\"tbody \"><tr class=\"row \"><td class=\"entry align:center colname:col1 valign:middle \"></td>\n                        <td class=\"entry align:center colname:col2 valign:middle  tcp-2cf12d9e-e7d0-4683-b984-89484068f1b1\">Amount <span class=\"formatted_line_break delivery_mode:Both \"></span>invested</td>\n                        <td class=\"entry align:center colname:col3 valign:middle  tcp-103423ce-8f5e-47bc-9556-9d63ced83798\">Balance<span class=\"formatted_line_break delivery_mode:Both \"></span> increase</td>\n                      </tr><tr class=\"row \"><td class=\"entry align:center colname:col1 valign:middle \">Account A</td>\n                        <td class=\"entry align:center colname:col2 valign:middle  tcp-b31e2593-f5a4-4c74-844e-f2f07437038f\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;$500</td>\n                        <td class=\"entry align:center colname:col3 valign:middle  tcp-9fce35c0-725a-46e6-87c7-da3e701ce7b0\">6% annual interest</td>\n                      </tr><tr class=\"row \"><td class=\"entry align:center colname:col1 valign:middle \">Account B</td>\n                        <td class=\"entry align:center colname:col2 valign:middle  tcp-25747e21-2fcd-451a-a1d2-72f692c7db08\">$1,000</td>\n                        <td class=\"entry align:center colname:col3 valign:middle  tcp-e8a06ae9-3a3f-42c0-b8dd-b64944012d7f\">$25 per year</td>\n                      </tr></tbody></table></td>\n              </tr></tbody></table></div>\n      </div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Two investments were made as shown in the table above. The interest in Account A is compounded once per year. Which of the following is true about the investments?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p>Account A always earns more money per year than Account B.</p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p>Account A always earns less money per year than Account B.</p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p>Account A earns more money per year than Account B at first but eventually earns less money per year.</p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p>Account A earns less money per year than Account B at first but eventually earns more money per year.</p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"a","rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. Account A starts with $500 and earns interest at 6% per year, so in the first year Account A earns (500)(0.06) = $30, which is greater than the $25 that Account B earns that year. Compounding interest can be modeled by an increasing exponential function, so each year Account A will earn more money than it did the previous year. Therefore, each year Account A earns at least $30 in interest. Since Account B always earns $25 each year, Account A always earns more money per year than Account B.<p>Choices B and D are incorrect. Account A earns $30 in the first year, which is greater than the $25 Account B earns in the first year. Therefore, neither the statement that Account A always earns less money per year than Account B nor the statement that Account A earns less money than Account B at first can be true. Choice C is incorrect. Since compounding interest&nbsp;<!--StartFragment-->can be modeled by an <!--EndFragment-->increasing exponential function, each year Account A will earn more money than it did the previous year. Therefore, Account A always earns at least $30 per year, which is more than the $25 per year that Account B earns.</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959638,"updateDate":1691007959638}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959638, 1691007959638),
    ($SATQ$affb2315$SATQ$, $SATQ$f12a8c8c-3eef-4c55-a726-f411ff595181$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$c76b7d50-0ed5-4ecb-b346-f465f3345924$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.F.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Inference from sample statistics and margin of error $SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">There are <math alttext="55"><mn>55</mn>
</math> students in Spanish club. A sample of the Spanish club students was selected at random and asked whether they intend to enroll in a new study program. Of those surveyed, <math alttext="20 percent sign"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> responded that they intend to enroll in the study program. Based on this survey, which of the following is the best estimate of the total number of Spanish club students who intend to enroll in the study program?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a8cff078-5355-49e4-9e76-506ca4c85bb6","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"11\"><mn>11</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1f340179-597a-4f0a-871d-327755665e7f","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"a102ac34-219a-4142-b8b2-a2fe31aea5f4","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2c45bc80-1952-4978-aece-a2b0fa690cf4","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"55\"><mn>55</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["a8cff078-5355-49e4-9e76-506ca4c85bb6"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that&nbsp;<math alttext="20 percent sign"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> of the students surveyed responded that they intend to enroll in the study program. Therefore, the proportion of students in Spanish club who intend to enroll in the study program, based on the survey, is <math alttext="0.20"><mn>0.20</mn></math>. Since there are <math alttext="55"><mn>55</mn>
</math> total students in Spanish club, the best estimate for the total number of these students who intend to enroll in the study program is <math alttext="55 left parenthesis 0.20 right parenthesis"><mn>55</mn><mfenced><mn>0.20</mn></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext="11"><mn>11</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This is the best estimate for the percentage, rather than the total number, of students in Spanish club who intend to enroll in the study program.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the best estimate for the total number of Spanish club students who do not intend to enroll in the study program.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the total number of students in Spanish club.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"affb2315","external_id":"f12a8c8c-3eef-4c55-a726-f411ff595181","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"c76b7d50-0ed5-4ecb-b346-f465f3345924","uId":"03227496-d5ae-42f7-a86d-fc2f312edb51","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.F.","skill_desc":"Inference from sample statistics and margin of error ","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">There are <math alttext=\"55\"><mn>55</mn>\n</math> students in Spanish club. A sample of the Spanish club students was selected at random and asked whether they intend to enroll in a new study program. Of those surveyed, <math alttext=\"20 percent sign\"><mn>20</mn><mo>%</mo></math> responded that they intend to enroll in the study program. Based on this survey, which of the following is the best estimate of the total number of Spanish club students who intend to enroll in the study program?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"a8cff078-5355-49e4-9e76-506ca4c85bb6","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"11\"><mn>11</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1f340179-597a-4f0a-871d-327755665e7f","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"20\"><mn>20</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"a102ac34-219a-4142-b8b2-a2fe31aea5f4","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"44\"><mn>44</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2c45bc80-1952-4978-aece-a2b0fa690cf4","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><math alttext=\"55\"><mn>55</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["a8cff078-5355-49e4-9e76-506ca4c85bb6"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that&nbsp;<math alttext=\"20 percent sign\"><mn>20</mn><m