ke:#000000;\" x=\"221.937262\" xlink:href=\"#me5cc95f241\" y=\"50.512714\"></use>\n    </g>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"p67365a6d96\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"262.488358\" x=\"27.497696\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for scatterplot\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>The scatterplot has 8 data points.</li>\n<li>The data points are in a linear pattern trending up from left to right.</li>\n<li>The data points have the following coordinates:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(1 comma 0)</li>\n<li>(2 comma 10)</li>\n<li>(3 comma 21)</li>\n<li>(4 comma 40)</li>\n<li>(5 comma 46)</li>\n<li>(6 comma 60)</li>\n<li>(7 comma 76)</li>\n<li>(8 comma 85)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">What was the weight, to the nearest pound, of all nectarines that grew on the tree during the <math alttext=\"4th\"><mn>4</mn><mtext>th</mtext></math> growing season after the tree's transplantation?</p>","type":"spr","correct_answer":["40"]},"createDate":1730147357405,"updateDate":1730147357405}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147357405, 1730147357405),
    ($SATQ$b5bc47d5$SATQ$, $SATQ$ec4a70f3-71cf-4dca-9776-c588830c5d34$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Problem-Solving and Data Analysis$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q$SATQ$, $SATQ$Q.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 7, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">In a scale model of an office building, a length of <math alttext="1"><mn>1</mn>
</math> inch is equivalent to a length of <math alttext="StartFraction 17 Over 3 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> feet in the actual office building. If a length in the actual office building measures <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> feet, which expression represents the corresponding length, in inches, in the model in terms of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"04647ce3-3911-4f2d-9386-bb68726def3a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 3 x Over left parenthesis 17 right parenthesis left parenthesis 12 right parenthesis EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mn>17</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>12</mn></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"466014d2-d90e-482f-9e93-b13263f21549","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 17 x Over left parenthesis 12 right parenthesis left parenthesis 3 right parenthesis EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mn>12</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"3d032cc3-72e4-4762-8e0a-ea91f42d9392","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 3 x Over 17 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>17</mn></mfrac></math></p>"},{"id":"ec4c7fb5-c399-47fc-824a-2891d16e29a9","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 17 x Over 3 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>17</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["3d032cc3-72e4-4762-8e0a-ea91f42d9392"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. It&rsquo;s given that in a scale model, a length of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> inch is equivalent to a length of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 17 Over 3 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> feet in the actual office building. This means that the ratio of a length, in feet, in the actual office building to the corresponding length, in inches, in the model is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 17 Over 3 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math>. Therefore, the length, in inches, in the model corresponding to a length in the actual office building of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> feet can be found by dividing <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 17 Over 3 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. Dividing by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 17 Over 3 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> is equivalent to multiplying by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="three seventeenths"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>17</mn></mfrac></math>, so the corresponding length, in inches, in the model in terms of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> can be represented by the expression <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 3 x Over 17 EndFraction"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>17</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect. This expression represents the corresponding length, in inches, in the model in terms of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> for a model where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1"><mn>1</mn></math> inch in the model is equivalent to a length of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="three seventeenths"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>17</mn></mfrac></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartFraction 17 Over 3 EndFraction"><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, feet in the actual building.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"b5bc47d5","external_id":"ec4a70f3-71cf-4dca-9776-c588830c5d34","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"38f48b3a-19a1-4bc0-b1a8-a6ef98f6a8be","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.A.","skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":7,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">In a scale model of an office building, a length of <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> inch is equivalent to a length of <math alttext=\"StartFraction 17 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> feet in the actual office building. If a length in the actual office building measures <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> feet, which expression represents the corresponding length, in inches, in the model in terms of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"04647ce3-3911-4f2d-9386-bb68726def3a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"StartFraction 3 x Over left parenthesis 17 right parenthesis left parenthesis 12 right parenthesis EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mfenced><mn>17</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mn>12</mn>