n>17</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>. Dividing by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 17 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math> is equivalent to multiplying by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"three seventeenths\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>17</mn></mfrac></math>, so the corresponding length, in inches, in the model in terms of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> can be represented by the expression <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 3 x Over 17 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>17</mn></mfrac></math>.</p>\n<p>Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>\n<p>Choice D is incorrect. This expression represents the corresponding length, in inches, in the model in terms of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> for a model where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn></math> inch in the model is equivalent to a length of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"three seventeenths\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>17</mn></mfrac></math>, not <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"StartFraction 17 Over 3 EndFraction\"><mfrac><mn>17</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math>, feet in the actual building.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1776362727993,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"b5bc47d5","skill_cd":"Q.A.","score_band_range_cd":7,"skill_desc":"Ratios, rates, proportional relationships, and units","createDate":1776362727993,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"","external_id":"ec4a70f3-71cf-4dca-9776-c58883