</math> is <math alttext="p percent sign"><mi>p</mi><mo>%</mo></math> greater than <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math>. It follows that <math alttext="140 equals 10 plus left parenthesis StartFraction p Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis 10"><mn>140</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mi>p</mi><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mn>10</mn></math>, which is equivalent to <math alttext="140 equals 10 plus StartFraction 10 Over 100 EndFraction p"><mn>140</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>10</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac><mi>p</mi></math>, or <math alttext="140 equals 10 plus 0.1 p"><mn>140</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mi>p</mi></math>. Subtracting <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math> from each side of this equation yields <math alttext="130 equals 0.1 p"><mn>130</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn><mi>p</mi></math>. Dividing each side of this equation by <math alttext="0.1"><mn>0.1</mn></math> yields <math alttext="1,300 equals p"><mn>1,300</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>p</mi></math>, or <math alttext="p equals 1,300"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1,300</mn></math>.</p>
