<p style="text-align: left;">At a distance of <math alttext="4,000"><mn>4,000</mn>
</math> feet above sea level, what is the temperature, <math alttext="in degree upper F"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mtext>F</mtext></math>, predicted by the line of best fit?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"85b010a1-5b53-43d0-b296-59d7aaccc389","content":"<p><math alttext=\"47\"><mn>47</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7da6f449-c738-4d6b-a59f-ce4ef2d2589e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"25cb87de-4907-4f79-b078-feaacbf809b4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"fceb29bb-d650-4d7c-b67b-5ab6fed3a567","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["7da6f449-c738-4d6b-a59f-ce4ef2d2589e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. In the given scatterplot, the <em>x</em>-values represent the distance above sea level, in feet, and the <em>y</em>-values represent the temperature, in <math alttext="degree upper F"><mo>&deg;</mo><mtext>F</mtext></math>. The point on the line of best fit with an <em>x</em>-value of <math alttext="4,000"><mn>4,000</mn>
</math> has a corresponding <em>y</em>-value of <math alttext="35"><mn>35</mn>
</math>. Therefore, at a distance of <math alttext="4,000"><mn>4,000</mn></math> feet above sea level, the temperature predicted by the line of best fit is <math alttext="35 degree upper F"><mn>35</mn><mo>&deg;</mo><mtext>F</mtext></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the temperature, in <math alttext="degree upper F"><mo>&deg;</mo><mtext>F</mtext></math>, predicted by the line of best fit at a distance of <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math> feet above sea level.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the measured temperature, in <math alttext="degree upper F"><mo>&deg;</mo><mtext>F</mtext></math>, at a distance of <math alttext="6,000"><mn>6,000</mn></math> feet above sea level.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"bc59c2d9","external_id":"be404513-86c1-473f-9573-d0ef7f6ac666","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"e9f3c0f6-4cc8-417b-9496-125e7eba5290","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"Q","domain":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","skill_cd":"Q.D.","skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The scatterplot shows the temperature, <math alttext=\"in degrees Fahrenheit left parenthesis degree upper F right parenthesis\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>degrees</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>Fahrenheit</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#176;</mo><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math>, and the distance above sea level, in feet, measured at <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> locations on Mount Jefferson. A line of best fit is also shown.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg version=\"1.0.0\" width=\"370px\" height=\"283.203125px\" viewBox=\"0 0 370 283.203125\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-label=\"A scatterplot in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis is labeled Distance above sea level, in feet. It ranges from 0 to 8,000. The y axis is labeled Temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit. It ranges from 0 to 80. Refer to long description.\"><defs><marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 -3 10 6\" markerUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" markerWidth=\"10px\" markerHeight=\"6px\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,-3 L10,0 L0,3\" fill=\"currentColor\"></path></marker></defs><g class=\"graph-group\" transform=\"translate(129.125, 25)\"><g class=\"grid-group\"><g class=\"x-grid\"><line x1=\"0.5\" y1=\"207.20312