ine stroke=\"currentColor\" x2=\"6px\" x1=\"-6px\" stroke-width=\"1px\"></line><text fill=\"currentColor\" x=\"-8\" dy=\"0.32em\" style=\"font-family: Noto Serif; font-size: 15px;\">80</text></g><line class=\"y-axis-line\" y1=\"222.203125\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5px\"></line><line class=\"y-axis-line\" y1=\"222.203125\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5px\" marker-end=\"url(#arrow)\"></line><text class=\"y-axis-label\" style=\"text-anchor: middle; dominant-baseline: text-after-edge; font-family: Noto Serif; font-style: italic; fill: currentColor; font-size: 15px;\" transform=\"translate(0,-12)\">y</text></g><text x=\"0\" y=\"207.203125\" dx=\"-13.25px\" dy=\"13.5px\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-size: 15px; font-style: italic; font-family: Noto Serif;\">O</text><path d=\"M0,91.811L207.199,157.585\" stroke=\"black\" stroke-width=\"2px\" fill=\"none\" stroke-dasharray=\"none\"></path><circle cx=\"23.202433268229168\" cy=\"89.35634765625001\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"46.404866536458336\" cy=\"113.90775960286459\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"69.6072998046875\" cy=\"113.90775960286459\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"116.01216634114584\" cy=\"121.27318318684895\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"139.214599609375\" cy=\"145.82459513346353\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle><circle cx=\"162.41703287760419\" cy=\"143.3694539388021\" r=\"4px\" fill=\"currentColor\"></circle></g><g class=\"xtitle-group\" transform=\"translate(232.7265625, 263.203125)\"><text class=\"xtitle-group-line-0\" transform=\"translate(0, 0)\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-family: Noto Serif; font-size: 15px; text-anchor: middle; dominant-baseline: hanging;\">Distance above sea level (feet)</text></g><g class=\"ytitle-group\" transform=\"translate(47.0625, 118.6015625)\"><text class=\"ytitle-group-line-0\" transform=\"translate(0, 0)\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-family: Noto Serif; font-size: 15px; text-anchor: middle; dominant-baseline: text-before-edge;\">Temperature</text><text class=\"ytitle-group-line-1\" transform=\"translate(0, 20)\" fill=\"currentColor\" style=\"font-family: Noto Serif; font-size: 15px; text-anchor: middle; dominant-baseline: text-before-edge;\">  (°F)</text></g></svg><div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for scatterplot\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul>\n<li>The scatterplot has 6 data points.</li>\n<li>The data points are in a linear pattern trending down from left to right.</li>\n<li>A line of best fit is shown:<br/>\n<ul>\n<li>The line of best fit slants down from left to right.</li>\n<li>The line of best fit passes through the following coordinates:<br/>\n<ul>\n<li>(0 comma 47)</li>\n<li>(4,000 comma 35)</li>\n<li>(7,000 comma 26)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">At a distance of <math alttext=\"4,000\"><mn>4,000</mn>\n</math> feet above sea level, what is the temperature, <math alttext=\"in degree upper F\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#176;</mo><mtext>F</mtext></math>, predicted by the line of best fit?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"85b010a1-5b53-43d0-b296-59d7aaccc389","content":"<p><math alttext=\"47\"><mn>47</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"7da6f449-c738-4d6b-a59f-ce4ef2d2589e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"25cb87de-4907-4f79-b078-feaacbf809b4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"25\"><mn>25</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"fceb29bb-d650-4d7c-b67b-5ab6fed3a567","content":"<p><math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["7da6f449-c738-4d6b-a59f-ce4ef2d2589e"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. In the given scatterplot, the <em>x</em>-values represent the distance above sea level, in feet, and the <em>y</em>-values represent the temperature, in <math alttext=\"degree upper F\"><mo>&deg;</mo><mtext>F</mtext></math>. The point on the line of best fit with an <em>x</em>-value of <math alttext=\"4,000\"><mn>4,000</mn>\n</math> has a corresponding <em>y</em>-value of <math alttext=\"35\"><mn>35</mn>\n</math>. Therefore, at a distance of <math alttext=\"4,000\"><mn>4,000</mn></math> feet above sea level, the temperature predicted by the line of best fit is <math alttext=\"35 degree upper F\"><mn>35</mn><mo>&deg;</mo><mtext>F</mtext></math>.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect. This is the temperature, in <math alttext=\"degree upper F\"><mo>&deg;</mo><mtext>F</mtext></math>, predicted by the line of best fit at a distance of <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math> feet above sea level.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is incorrect. This is the measured temperature, in <math alttext=\"degree upper F\"><mo>&deg;</mo><mtext>F</mtext></math>, at a distance of <math alttext=\"6,000\"><mn>6,000</mn></math> feet above sea level.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1743430554986,"pPcc":"SAT#Q","questionId":"bc59c2d9","skill_cd":"Q.D.","score_band_range_cd":1,"skill_desc":"Two-variable data: Models and scatterplots","createDate":1743430554986,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Problem-Solving and Data Analysis","ibn":"","external_id":"be404513-86c1-473f-9573-d0ef7f6ac666","primary_class_cd":"Q","uId":"e9f3c0f6-4cc8-417b-9496-125e7eba5290","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The scatterplot shows the temperature, <math alttext=\"in degrees Fahrenheit left parenthesis degree upper F right parenthesis\"><mtext>in</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>degrees</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>Fahrenheit</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#176;</mo><mtext>F</mtext></mrow></mfenced></math>, and the distance above sea level, in feet, measured at <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> locations on Mount Jefferson. A line of best fit is also shown.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><figure class='image'><svg version=\"1.0.0\" width=\"370px\" height=\"283.203125px\" viewBox=\"0 0 370 283.203125\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" role=\"img\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" aria-label=\"A scatterplot in the x y plane with the origin labeled O. The x axis is labeled Distance above sea level, in feet. It ranges from 0 to 8,000. The y axis is labeled Temperature, in degrees Fahrenheit. It ranges from 0 to 80. Refer to long description.\"><defs><marker id=\"arrow\" viewBox=\"0 -3 10 6\" markerUnits=\"userSpaceOnUse\" markerWidth=\"10px\" markerHeight=\"6px\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0,-3 L10,0 L0,3\" fill=\"currentColor\"></path></marker></defs><g class=\"graph-group\" transform=\"translate(129.125, 25)\"><g class=\"grid-group\"><g class=\"x-grid\"><line x1=\"0.5\" y1=\"207.203125\" x2=\"0.5\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#757576\" stroke-width=\"0\" class=\"x-grid\"></line><line x1=\"0.5\" y1=\"207.203125\" x2=\"0.5\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#757576\" stroke-width=\"0\" class=\"x-grid\"></line><line x1=\"23.702433268229168\" y1=\"207.203125\" x2=\"23.702433268229168\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#757576\" stroke-width=\"1px\" class=\"x-grid\"></line><line x1=\"46.904866536458336\" y1=\"207.203125\" x2=\"46.904866536458336\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#757576\" stroke-width=\"1px\" class=\"x-grid\"></line><line x1=\"70.1072998046875\" y1=\"207.203125\" x2=\"70.1072998046875\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#757576\" stroke-width=\"1px\" class=\"x-grid\"></line><line x1=\"93.30973307291667\" y1=\"207.203125\" x2=\"93.30973307291667\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#757576\" stroke-width=\"1px\" class=\"x-grid\"></line><line x1=\"116.51216634114584\" y1=\"207.203125\" x2=\"116.51216634114584\" y2=\"0\" stroke=\"#757576\" stroke-width=\"1px\" class=\"x-grid\"></line><line x1=